UPDATE companies SET description='J M Mold South Inc., doing business as JMMS, was founded in 1986 by David M. Bowers in Easley, South Carolina. Bowers II, became chief executive officer and his daughter, Michelle Powell, became chief operating officer. The firm maintains its headquarters in Easley and operates engineering and tool-making facilities in Dong Guan, China.

JMMS provides total program management for die casting and injection molding tooling, covering thermoplastic injection molding, thermoset injection and compression/transfer molding, and die cast tooling. Its services span design validation, concurrent engineering, Advanced Product Quality Planning (APQP), project management, troubleshooting, and mold maintenance. The company uses a Cimatron 13.0 CAD/CAM platform to integrate communications, collaboration, and program management across its global operations.

The company serves original equipment manufacturers and Tier vendors in the automotive, medical technology, and consumer products sectors. In consumer products, JMMS has produced molded components for microwaves, mixers, blenders, refrigerators, icemakers, and air deflection systems. A 2016 partnership with the Moldetipo Group expanded its reach into the global automotive market.

JMMS emphasizes single-source accountability, combining design, engineering, manufacturing, and maintenance under one roof. The company states that its next-generation tooling approach delivers standardized, repeatable processes that meet OEM quality benchmarks and lead times while lowering total cost of ownership, backed by an ISO 9001:2015 registered quality management system.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Total program management", "Die casting tooling design and manufacturing", "Plastic injection molding tooling design and manufacturing", "Thermoplastic injection molding tooling", "Thermoset injection and compression/transfer tooling", "Tooling engineering and design validation", "Concurrent engineering", "Advanced Product Quality Planning (APQP)", "Injection molding troubleshooting", "Die cast tooling venting and temperature control correction", "Porosity reduction in die cast parts", "Project management (dedicated project managers per discipline)", "Mold and die maintenance", "Single-source tooling procurement"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical Technologies", "Consumer Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Cimatron 13.0 CAD/CAM platform"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Total program management covering design, engineering, manufacturing, and maintenance for die casting and injection molding tooling", "Single-source accountability across the tooling lifecycle", "ISO 9001:2015 registered quality management system", "Cimatron 13.0 platform for integrated communications, collaboration, and program management", "Global footprint with U.S. headquarters and China tool-making operations"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 by David M. Bowers -> /about", "Second-generation leadership 2008 (David M. Bowers II CEO, Michelle Powell COO) -> /about", "Headquarters Easley, SC; operations in Dong Guan, China -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> / and /about", "Total program management for die casting and injection molding tooling -> /", "Services: thermoplastic injection molding, thermoset injection & compression/transfer, die casting tooling -> /", "Engineering: design validation, concurrent engineering, APQP -> /", "Troubleshooting for injection molding and die casting -> /", "Cimatron 13.0 platform for communications and collaboration -> /about", "Industries: automotive, medical technologies, consumer products -> / and /about", "Consumer product examples: microwave, mixer, blender, refrigerator, icemaker, air deflection components -> /", "Moldetipo Group partnership for global automotive market -> /", "Single-source accountability: design, engineering, manufacturing, maintenance -> /", "Family-owned (implied by founder and children in leadership) -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We deliver total program management for thermoplastic injection molding, thermoset injection & compression/transfer, and die casting tooling.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/3478315/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-m-mold-south-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JC Biomedical was founded in 1997 in Omaha, Nebraska, as a privately owned biomedical equipment service company. The business began serving medical facilities and health care systems in the Omaha area and has since expanded its reach across the Midwest.

The company provides a full range of biomedical equipment services, including preventive maintenance, electrical safety inspections, equipment calibrations, repairs, pre-use inspections, equipment inventory management, and equipment sales. Its nationally certified technicians work on a wide variety of clinical devices, with specialization in cardiology, surgical, anesthesia, and general biomedical equipment. Services are performed on-site at hospitals, surgical centers, clinics, laboratories, and veterinary facilities.

JC Biomedical serves a diverse client base across the healthcare sector. Customers include large and small hospitals, outpatient surgery centers, medical clinics, research facilities, laboratories, and veterinarians. Long-term clients such as Miracle Hills Surgery Center and various outpatient surgery managers have relied on the company for over two decades for prompt repairs, detailed preventive maintenance programs, and regulatory compliance documentation.

The company emphasizes competitive pricing, local responsiveness, and technician expertise as its core differentiators. Its mission is to deliver timely repairs and calibrations at the most competitive prices in the Midwest, while helping clients eliminate costly manufacturer service contracts. Technicians also provide staff training on proper equipment operation and maintenance to increase patient safety and equipment longevity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Preventive Maintenance", "Electrical Safety Inspections", "Equipment Calibrations", "Equipment Repairs", "Pre-Use Inspections", "Equipment Inventory Management & Documentation", "Equipment Sales", "On-site Repair Services", "Staff Training on Equipment Operation and Maintenance"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Hospitals", "Surgical Centers", "Medical Clinics", "Laboratories", "Veterinarians"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nationally certified technicians on staff", "Local Omaha presence since 1997 with Midwest service area", "Competitive pricing below manufacturer service contract costs", "Flexible scheduling to minimize facility downtime", "Staff training on equipment operation and maintenance"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1997 -> db", "Headquarters in Omaha, Nebraska -> db", "Privately owned biomedical equipment service company -> db description", "Nationally certified technicians -> /about", "Services: preventive maintenance, electrical safety inspections, calibrations, repairs, pre-use inspections, inventory management, equipment sales -> /services", "Specializes in cardiology, surgical, anesthesia, general biomedical equipment -> /about", "Serves hospitals, surgical centers, clinics, laboratories, veterinarians -> /about and /services", "Mission: timely repairs and calibrations at competitive prices in the Midwest -> /about", "Local presence in Omaha since 1997 -> /about", "Flexible scheduling and staff training -> /services and /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "JC Biomedical is a privately owned comprehensive biomedical equipment service company.", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jc-biomedical-medical-equipment-repair-calibration' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JE Import Performance operates from a 60,000-square-foot facility in Baltimore, Maryland. The company was founded in 1998 with a mission to serve the performance needs of local car enthusiasts while providing dependable, honest automotive service. Over nearly three decades, that mission has grown into a full-service automotive center.

The shop delivers complete automotive care under one roof, covering maintenance, repair, and performance upgrades for import, domestic, and European vehicles. Services include brake system repair, climate control repair, engine diagnostics and repair, muffler and exhaust work, oil and filter changes, transmission and drivetrain service, timing belt and chain service, tire repair and installation, and wheel alignment. The facility also handles performance tuning and custom builds, drawing on racing-proven experience.

The customer base consists of Baltimore-area drivers and car enthusiasts who own import, domestic, or European vehicles, ranging from daily commuters to those pursuing ambitious performance builds.

The company emphasizes practical expertise and attention to detail, rooted in racing experience that translates directly into its performance service offerings.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Brake system repair", "Climate control system repair", "Engine repair & diagnostics testing", "Muffler and exhaust repair", "Oil change & filter service", "Transmission & drivetrain service", "Timing belt & timing chain service", "Tire repair & installation service", "Wheel alignment service", "Performance tuning and custom builds"], "industries": ["Automotive service and maintenance", "Automotive performance tuning"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["60,000 sq ft facility", "Racing-proven experience applied to performance services", "Import, domestic, and European vehicle expertise", "Complete automotive care (maintenance, repair, upgrades) under one roof", "Serving Baltimore drivers since 1998"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 -> db", "Baltimore, Maryland location -> db", "60,000 sq ft facility -> page /", "Import, domestic, European vehicle service -> page /", "Racing-proven experience -> page /", "Services: brake repair, climate control, engine diagnostics, muffler/exhaust, oil change, transmission, timing belt/chain, tire repair/install, wheel alignment, performance tuning/custom builds -> page /", "Serving Baltimore drivers since 1998 -> page /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Trusted automotive repair, diagnostics and performance expertise for import, domestic and European vehicles, all under one roof.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='je-import-performance-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JK Woodworking was founded in 2006 in Oak Ridge, New Jersey, located in Morris County. The business was established by a professional with a degree in Construction Management and two decades of experience in custom woodworking and home improvement. The founder has spent 15 years working in the field, building a practice around tailored wood fabrication and residential renovation.

