UPDATE companies SET description='JW Electrical Supply operates from Baltimore, Maryland, where it was founded in 1977. Leadership includes President Wajahat Ashai and Head of Marketing and Operations Suhail Kamran, though the original founders are not identified in public materials.

The firm stocks circuit breakers, fuses, safety switches, motor starters, connectors, transformers, and bus plugs from manufacturers such as Square D, General Electric, Appleton, Mersen, and Eaton. Inventory spans new, used, open-box surplus, and hard-to-find obsolete items, supporting both new installations and legacy system maintenance. Orders are fulfilled through an e-commerce platform with a small team of 1–10 employees; facility size and annual volume are not disclosed.

Customers include electrical contractors, industrial facilities, and MRO buyers across the United States. Testimonials cite projects for contractors such as Titan Electrical Contractors in Houston, Crown Manufacturing in Cleveland, and GreenTech Industrial Solutions in Atlanta, as well as plant engineers at Allied Equipment in Detroit and utility personnel at Northern Utility Services in Seattle.

The company states its mission is to eliminate supply-chain headaches by providing dependable delivery, responsive technical support, and cross-referencing expertise for hard-to-source parts. Since its founding, it has emphasized on-time shipping as a standard rather than a goal, and positions itself as a partner for both routine procurement and emergency legacy replacements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical supply distribution", "Surplus and obsolete equipment sourcing", "Nationwide shipping", "Technical support and part cross-referencing", "Custom ordering for specialty units", "E-commerce procurement", "Legacy system component supply"], "industries": ["Electrical contractors", "Industrial facilities", "Maintenance and MRO"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nationwide shipping from Baltimore headquarters", "Stocks new, used, surplus, and obsolete electrical components", "Specializes in hard-to-find legacy and discontinued parts", "E-commerce platform with technical support for part cross-referencing", "Carries major brands including Square D, GE, Appleton, Mersen, Eaton"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1977 -> home page ''Since 1977'' and db", "Headquartered in Baltimore, Maryland -> db and about-us page", "Distributes circuit breakers, fuses, safety switches, motor starters, connectors, transformers, bus plugs -> description and home page", "Carries new, used, surplus, obsolete inventory -> description and about-us page", "Brands: Square D, GE, Appleton, Mersen, Eaton -> about-us page", "Nationwide shipping -> description and capabilities", "Employee count 1-10 -> db", "Industries: electrical contractors, industrial facilities, maintenance/MRO -> description and industries_served", "Customer examples from testimonials -> home page testimonials", "Mission: eliminate supply-chain headaches, dependable delivery, technical support -> home page and about-us page", "Leadership: Wajahat Ashai (President), Suhail Kamran (Head Marketing and Operations) -> about-us page", "E-commerce platform -> about-us page"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "JW Electrical Supply is a Maryland-based distributor of industrial and commercial electrical supplies", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "1-10", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jw-electrical-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Jagemann Precision Plastics operates in Murfreesboro, Tennessee, as a division of Jagemann Stamping Co., a fourth-generation family-owned business founded in 1946 by William P. Jagemann, Sr. in Manitowoc, Wisconsin. The division was established to specialize in insert molding and over molding, combining metal and plastic components into single composite pieces.

The company focuses on insert molding and over molding processes for automotive components, solar connectors, and electrical parts. A 2015 expansion added 30,000 square feet and up to 90 jobs at the Murfreesboro facility, complementing the parent company’s 200,000-square-foot plant in Manitowoc with more than 70 presses ranging from 15 to 700 tons. In-house tooling design, build, and maintenance support deep draw stamping, fineblanking, and progressive die stamping, while secondary operations such as deburring, pressure testing, washing, and machining are performed under one roof.

Jagemann Precision Plastics serves the automotive, appliance, solar, and medical markets, along with broader industrial, consumer, and electrical manufacturing sectors. Customers include Tier 1 suppliers and OEMs seeking to reduce assembly time, labor, and cost through integrated metal-plastic components.

The company emphasizes a collaborative, engineering-driven approach, with leadership citing in-house tooling, rapid response, and a quality system certified to ISO 9001:2015 and IATF 16949 as key differentiators. The integrated setup aims to eliminate handoffs, maintain tight process control, and deliver consistent high-volume production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Insert molding", "Over molding", "Deep draw stamping", "Fineblanking", "Progressive die stamping", "In-house tool design and build", "Tool maintenance", "Bending", "Belt sanding", "Tumbling and deburring", "Pressure testing", "Visual inspection", "Washing and cleaning", "Production machining", "Automated vision inspection", "SPC monitoring"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Appliance", "Solar", "Medical", "Industrial", "Consumer", "Electrical"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel (304, 305, 316, 430, 434)", "Cold Rolled Steel (1010, 1018, 1020, 1030, 1040, 1050)", "Hot Rolled Steel", "Carbon Steel", "High Carbon Steel (1035)", "High Strength Low Alloy (HSLA)", "Aluminum (3003, 5052, 6061, 6062)", "Brass (80-20, 85-15, 70-30)", "Bronze", "Copper", "Galvanized Steel", "Nickel and Tin Pre-Plated Steel", "Inconel", "Red Metal", "Titanium"], "equipment": ["70+ presses (15 to 700 tons)", "Transfer presses", "Progressive presses", "Fineblanking presses", "Automated data collection system at press site", "Vision inspection systems"], "volume": "High-volume production (thousands to millions of parts)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Insert molding combining metal and plastic into a single composite piece", "Over molding for automotive components, solar connectors, and electrical parts", "In-house tool design, build, and maintenance", "Integrated secondary operations (deburring, pressure testing, washing, machining) under one roof", "Quality management certified to ISO 9001:2015 and IATF 16949"], "facts_used": ["Location: Murfreesboro, Tennessee -> db", "Parent company founded 1946 by William P. Jagemann, Sr. -> /about", "Family-owned, fourth-generation -> /about", "Insert molding and over molding specialization -> /", "2015 expansion: 30,000 sq ft, up to 90 jobs -> /", "Parent facility: 200,000 sq ft, 70+ presses 15-700 tons -> /capabilities", "In-house tooling design, build, maintenance -> /capabilities", "Secondary operations: deburring, pressure testing, washing, machining -> /capabilities", "Industries: automotive, appliance, solar, medical, industrial, consumer, electrical -> /, /about", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, IATF 16949 -> /quality", "Materials list -> /capabilities", "Volume: thousands to millions of parts -> /quality", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Jagemann Precision Plastics specializes in insert molding that combines discrete components, including metal and plastics into a single composite piece.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/jagemann-stamping-company/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jagemann-precision-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Jam Packaging, a family-owned business, has operated from St. Louis, Missouri since its founding in 1973. The company began as a manufacturer and distributor of plastic bags for a broad range of industrial and commercial customers.

Today the firm produces an extensive line of plastic bags—including t-shirt, poly, gusseted, resealable, garment, merchandise, retail, doorknob, and newspaper styles—while also stocking more than 10,000 packaging and shipping items such as tapes, labels, bubble wrap, mailers, boxes, and custom-printed bags. The catalog lists roughly 20,000 items in stock, all marked as made in the United States, with an emphasis on rapid order fulfillment.

The customer base spans retail, shipping, packaging, and office-supply sectors, with products like cash-register paper, price-marking labelers, retail signage, and shipping labels tailored to those markets.

Jam Packaging states its guiding goal is to keep shipping and packaging supply costs as low as possible, differentiating itself through domestic manufacturing, a large in-stock inventory, and fast delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic bag manufacturing", "Custom printing on bags", "Packaging and shipping supply distribution", "Large-scale inventory stocking (10,000+ SKUs)", "Rapid order fulfillment"], "industries": ["Retail", "Shipping", "Packaging", "Office supplies", "E-commerce"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 10,000 products stocked for immediate shipment", "20,000 items available in inventory", "All products made in the USA", "Fast delivery on stocked items", "Family-owned since 1973"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1973 -> db", "Family-owned business -> /", "Headquartered in St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Manufactures plastic bags (t-shirt, poly, gusseted, resealable, garment, merchandise, retail, doorknob, newspaper) -> /", "Stocks over 10,000 packaging and shipping products -> /", "Approximately 20,000 items in stock -> /", "Products made in USA -> /", "Fast delivery emphasized -> /", "Offers custom printed bags -> /", "Goal to keep shipping and packaging supply costs low -> /", "Product categories include adhesive tapes, closeouts, fragile labels, labelers, packaging supplies, shipping supplies, stock bags -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1973, Jam Packaging- a family business, has been manufacturing and distributing plastic bags for various industries.", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jam-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Jason Lewis Furniture was founded in 2001 in Chicago, Illinois, by Jason Lewis. Lewis grew up in a Midwestern family of engineers and builders and began woodworking as a child. He apprenticed with a local woodworker before establishing his own studio. The company operates from a showroom and studio in the Logan Square neighborhood.

The studio functions as a production woodworking and design shop, specializing in contemporary, finely made wood furniture and objects. It handles custom woodworking and fabrication, taking on custom projects while also producing an ongoing line of original furniture. The work draws on traditional fine woodworking techniques and midcentury design influences. No specific facility size, headcount, or volume figures are disclosed.

The business works directly with clients seeking heirloom-quality modern furniture and woodworking of all kinds.

Lewis started the studio to combine the traditional fine woodworking craft he learned as an apprentice with the simple midcentury design that first inspired him. The company emphasizes direct client collaboration and the creation of heirloom-quality pieces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Furniture fabrication", "Fine woodworking", "Custom furniture design", "Production woodworking"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct client collaboration on custom projects", "Heirloom-quality modern furniture", "Traditional fine woodworking techniques", "Midcentury design inspiration", "Ongoing line of original furniture designs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> db", "Headquarters Chicago, Illinois -> db", "Founder Jason Lewis -> /about", "Custom woodworking and fabrication -> /", "Production woodworking and design studio -> /", "Heirloom quality modern furniture -> /about", "Traditional fine woodworking technique -> /about", "Midcentury design inspiration -> /about", "Direct client collaboration -> /about", "Showroom and studio in Logan Square -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "A production woodworking and design studio specializing in contemporary, finely made wood furniture and objects.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jason-lewis-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Jeffries Manufacturing LLC operates from Charlton Heights, West Virginia, where Randall Jeffries founded the company in 2021. Jeffries, drawing on nearly three decades of personal welding and fabrication experience, identified a market gap for precision-crafted frame plates for first-generation Toyota Tundra trucks and launched the business to fill it. The venture began with a focus on American-made durability and innovation.

The company produces a line of proprietary products including bolt-in frame supports for Tundra pickups, lower housing guards for Mercury, Evinrude, Honda, and Yamaha outboard motors, a patented propeller guard developed for high-water rescue, and the J-Stop™ anti-pest garage door bracket. In addition to its own product line, Jeffries Manufacturing provides a full suite of metal fabrication and welding services—MIG, TIG, arc, aluminum, stainless steel, flux-cored, and structural welding—along with sheet metal design, equipment and machinery repair, heavy equipment and truck frame repair, and Caterpillar excavator implement installations, hydraulic hammer rebuilds, and quick coupler installations.

Customers span marine, automotive, fire and rescue, heavy equipment, and pest control sectors. The Glasgow Fire Department partners with the firm for its patented propeller guard used in high-water rescue operations. The company also serves truck owners needing frame reinforcement, boaters requiring lower unit protection, and construction firms needing CAT excavator maintenance. Jeffries Manufacturing emphasizes local sourcing, purchasing steel from West Virginia vendors and supporting community projects.

The company differentiates itself as the sole manufacturer of its Tundra frame plate design and holds a patent on its rescue propeller guard. Its foundation rests on Jeffries’ 29-plus years of welding expertise, a commitment to safety and creative problem solving, and a business model built on reliable service and respect for clients.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Arc welding", "Aluminum welding", "Aesthetic welding", "Stainless steel welding", "Flux-cored arc welding", "Structural welding", "Sheet metal design", "Equipment repair", "Machinery repair", "Product design", "Heavy equipment repair", "Truck frame repair", "Manufacturing operations management", "CAT excavator implement installations", "CAT hydraulic hammer rebuilds", "CAT excavator quick coupler installations"], "industries": ["Marine", "Automotive", "Fire and rescue", "Heavy equipment", "Pest control"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only manufacturer of precision-crafted Tundra frame plates", "Patented propeller guard for high-water rescue applications", "Over 29 years of welding and fabrication experience", "Steel sourced from West Virginia vendors", "Focus on safety and creative problem solving"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2021 by Randall Jeffries -> /about", "Located in Charlton Heights, West Virginia -> db", "Products: Tundra frame supports, outboard motor lower housing guards, patented propeller guard, J-Stop anti-pest bracket -> /", "Processes: metal fabrication, MIG/TIG/arc/aluminum/stainless/flux-cored/structural welding, sheet metal design, equipment/machinery/heavy equipment/truck frame repair, CAT excavator services -> /about", "Partnership with Glasgow Fire Department for patented propeller guard used in high-water rescue -> /about", "Over 29 years of welding and fabrication experience -> /about", "Sources steel from West Virginia vendors -> /about", "Only manufacturers of Tundra frame plates -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "To this day, we are the only manufacturers of this type of product.", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jeffries-manufacturing-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The privately owned company began by producing a proprietary flooring system for the agricultural industry before expanding into custom injection molding for other customers.

The company operates a 40,000-square-foot facility in Allendale housing 16 injection molding presses ranging from 110 to 1,100 tons, supported by a staff of 60. It runs low, medium, and high volumes daily across multiple materials, offering injection molding, insert molding, and over molding. Jimdi also manages tooling from engineering through tryout, maintains relationships with domestic and offshore tool shops, and provides engineering support for material selection. Secondary operations include automated and manual assembly cells, sonic welding, silk screening, pad printing, and laser etching.

Jimdi serves agriculture, automotive, consumer products, office furniture, and recreation markets.

