UPDATE companies SET description='Jonathan A. Nussbaum established his furniture-making practice in Portland, Oregon, in 2009 after a three-year apprenticeship with German Master Furniture Maker Kai Fuhrmann. The sole proprietor began with hand tools, gradually incorporating modern machinery as he mastered each traditional technique, a philosophy that still guides the one-person shop today.

The shop produces custom furniture across dining, living, bedroom, and office categories — tables, chairs, benches, case goods, beds, desks, and conference tables — using locally sourced, responsibly managed hardwoods such as Oregon White Oak, Big Leaf Maple, American Cherry, and Western Walnut. Work combines time-honored joinery with both hand and machine processes, yielding one-off pieces built to heirloom standards in a modest Portland facility.

The maker collaborates closely on design, wood movement, and finish details throughout each project.

Nussbaum cites his apprenticeship foundation, commitment to environmental responsibility, and the ability to give each client undivided attention as the reasons the business exists. The one-person structure ensures direct communication from concept through delivery, with the maker overseeing every joint, surface, and installation himself.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Joinery", "Hand tool woodworking", "Machine woodworking", "Wood finishing", "Wood sourcing (local, responsible)", "Custom casework", "Custom table making", "Custom seating", "Custom bed making", "Custom storage design"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Office furniture", "Custom woodworking"], "materials": ["Oregon White Oak", "Big Leaf Maple", "American Cherry", "Western Walnut", "Locally sourced hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Apprenticeship with German Master Furniture Maker Kai Fuhrmann (2006\u20132009)", "Custom furniture built with time-honored joinery and mixed hand/machine methods", "Locally sourced, responsibly managed hardwoods only", "One-person operation providing direct client attention throughout", "Heirloom-quality pieces designed for generational use"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 -> db, /", "Located in Portland, Oregon -> /", "Sole proprietor Jonathan Nussbaum -> /", "Apprenticed under Kai Fuhrmann 2006-2009 -> /", "One-person operation -> /", "Uses locally sourced, responsibly managed wood -> /", "Offers dining, living, bedroom, office furniture -> /", "Materials: Oregon White Oak, Big Leaf Maple, American Cherry, Western Walnut -> /", "Customer reviews describe custom dining table, bed, board game table, jewelry box -> /", "Shop address and phone -> / (not used in profile)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Designing and building custom furniture rooted in exceptional workmanship, time honored joinery techniques, environmental responsibility and attention to client desires, from locally sourced, responsibly managed wood since 2009.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "1", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jonathan-a-nussbaum-furniture-maker' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Jones Creek Apparel opened in 2010 in Winterset, Iowa, with a commitment to provide custom apparel backed by personal service that larger vendors could not match. The company operates from its own facility and also serves the Des Moines metro through a sub-brand, Waukee Ink.

The shop produces screen printing, embroidery, and direct-to-film (DTF) printing entirely in-house, while sublimated jerseys and promotional products are sourced through partners but held to the same quality standard. The company decorates garments from brands such as Nike, Under Armour, New Era, and Gildan, and states it handles orders ranging from six pieces to 600 pieces with the same attention.

Clients include businesses, schools, sports teams, and organizations across Central Iowa. Examples cited by the company include Farmers & Merchants State Bank and various local teams and small businesses seeking corporate uniforms, team apparel, event giveaways, and corporate gifts.

