UPDATE companies SET description='KAM Plastics Corp was founded in 1994 in Holland, Michigan, by Paul Kalkman and Cleon Morgan.

The company specializes in plastic injection molding and assembly, operating over 50 molding machines across facilities in Holland, Michigan, and Arteaga, Mexico (via the KAMEX joint venture). Capabilities include two-shot molding, insert molding, and value-added processes such as chrome plating, painting, and pad printing. A product development and launch team supports customers from concept through production.

KAM serves automotive (Tier 2 and below), furniture, military, recreational vehicle, and consumer product markets. Early projects included the Ford Roll Up Window Handle (1995) and the Ford Ground Illumination Light Module (2000), and the company notes its parts can be found on products from U.S. companies.

The company emphasizes solving complex molding challenges — "We do the hard stuff" — and cites its employee-ownership culture, quality systems (IATF 16949:2016, ISO 9001), and tools like CMM inspection, 3D scanning, and 8D problem solving as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO 9001','ISO/TS 16949:2009']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Assembly", "Two-shot molding", "Insert molding", "Chrome plating", "Painting", "Pad printing", "Product development and launch support", "Custom gaging", "3D scanning", "8D problem solving", "Design of Experiments (DOE)", "Gage R&R studies", "Mistake proofing (poka-yoke)", "PPAP submissions", "ERP (Global Shop Solutions)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Furniture", "Military", "Recreational vehicle", "Consumer products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CMM (Coordinate Measuring Machine)", "3D scanning equipment", "Custom gaging fixtures", "Injection molding machines (50+)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2004", "IATF 16949:2016 and ISO 9001 certified quality management", "Two-shot and insert molding capabilities for complex assemblies", "Manufacturing facilities in both the U.S. and Mexico", "In-house quality tools including CMM, 3D scanning, and custom gaging"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 in Holland, Michigan by Paul Kalkman and Cleon Morgan -> /about", "Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2004, full ownership by 2012 -> /about", "Operates molding facilities in two countries (US and Mexico) with 50 machines -> /about", "Certified to IATF 16949:2016 (2018), ISO 9001 (2006), ISO/TS 16949:2009 (2014) -> /about, /quality", "Serves automotive (Tier 2 or lower), furniture, military, recreational vehicle, consumer products -> /about, /quality", "Processes: plastic injection molding, assembly, two-shot molding, insert molding, chrome plating, painting, pad printing -> /about, /quality", "Quality tools: CMM, 3D scanning, cust