UPDATE companies SET description='KG Sheet Metal Services, LLC is a commercial sheet metal contractor based in Upper Marlboro, Maryland. Founded in 2002 by Kevin Grenier, who began his sheet metal career in 1985, the company grew from a basement shop into one of the Washington, D.C. area''s most reliable commercial sheet metal contractors. It is a family-owned business, with Grenier as owner and president, later joined by co-owners Chris Berry (VP of Project Management) and Wes Willis (VP of Estimating).

The company provides custom fabrication and installation of sheet metal from a 30,000-square-foot facility. Its capabilities include ductwork and accessories, all-welded duct systems in galvanized, stainless, black iron, and aluminum, flues and breaching installation, FRP installation, certified fire damper inspections, duct air leakage testing, custom design-build assist, custom welding, and CADD/Autodesk 3D modeling. A dedicated Small Projects/Services Department handles expedited design, fabrication, and installation for smaller or emergency jobs. Union-certified Local 100 craftsmen perform the work using state-of-the-art equipment.

KG Sheet Metal serves government, industrial, and commercial clients. Project examples include the University of Maryland, Amtrak, Fort George G. Meade, the Washington Monument, Smithsonian National Zoological Park, Martin Luther King Jr. Elementary, Smithsonian National Air & Space Museum, The Mayflower Hotel, Virginia Hospital Center, and Walter Reed Military Medical Center. The firm works across hospitality, healthcare, military installations, government buildings, schools and universities, transportation, and national landmarks, often partnering with mechanical and general contractors.

The company emphasizes honest, expert, and expedient service, aiming to exceed expectations on every project. Its coordination team uses Autodesk software to create 3D models that catch issues early, and most projects are drawn and fabricated in-house to streamline installation. KG Sheet Metal has won multiple craftsmanship awards and highlights its ability to respond quickly through the Small Projects/Services Department, which was expanded in 2016 by merging with West Sheet Metal.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication", "Installation", "Ductwork & accessories", "All-welded duct systems (galvanized, stainless, black iron, aluminum)", "Flues/breaching installation", "FRP installation", "Certified fire damper inspections", "Duct air leakage testing", "Custom design-build assist", "Custom welding", "CADD/Autodesk 3D modeling", "Small projects/services (design, fabrication, installation)"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Healthcare", "Government", "Military", "Education", "Transportation", "Commercial", "Industrial", "National landmarks"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Stainless steel", "Black iron", "Aluminum", "FRP (fiberglass reinforced plastic)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30,000 SF fabrication facility", "Union-certified Local 100 sheet metal craftsmen", "In-house CADD/Autodesk 3D modeling", "Small Projects/Services Department for expedited design, fabrication, and installation", "Multiple craftsmanship awards"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 by Kevin Grenier -> db, /, /about-us", "Headquarters Upper Marlboro, MD -> db, /, /about-us", "Family-owned business -> / (\"longtime family business\")", "30,000 SF facility -> /, /services", "Union-certified Local 100 craftsmen -> /, /about-us", "Services: ductwork, welded duct systems, flues, FRP, fire damper inspections, leakage testing, design-build, welding, CADD -> /services", "Small Projects/Services Department expande