UPDATE companies SET description='Kalsec was founded in 1958 in Kalamazoo, Michigan, by Paul H. Todd, Jr., who declared, "We hold nature in awesome respect." The company remains family-owned and began as Vegetone Color Systems, pioneering custom natural color combinations and early use of gas-liquid chromatography for spice extraction.

Today Kalsec produces natural food and beverage ingredients across four platforms: natural colors, taste and sensory solutions, food protection, and hop products under the KalHops brand. Its vertically integrated supply chain runs from seed to shelf, supported by a global network of research, finishing, and distribution sites including the Don Berdahl Center for New Technology in Kalamazoo, the SPICE Lab at Wageningen University, and a new Spice Processing Center in Michigan. The company operates analytical labs equipped with gas chromatography–mass spectrometry and a patented vacuum fractionation process for hop oils.

Kalsec serves the food and beverage industry, with documented applications in beverages, fats and oils, flavors and seasoning blends, meat and poultry, noodles, pickles, plant-based proteins, refrigerated and prepared foods, sauces/dressings/condiments, and snacks. Its customers range from large global brands to craft brewers seeking consistent hop aroma and bitterness.

The company''s stated purpose is "unlocking the potential of people, nature & science to nourish the world." As a certified B Corp, it emphasizes social and environmental standards alongside its family-ownership model, positioning its vertically integrated supply chain and sensory expertise (Spectrum Method-trained panel) as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF certification','B Corp certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Natural color formulation and blending", "Natural taste and sensory solution development", "Natural food protection (antimicrobial/antioxidant systems)", "Hop extraction and hop product development (KalHops)", "Analytical testing (qualitative/quantitative, chemometrics, GC-MS, chromatography, rapid oxidation tests)", "Application development (dosing, recipe fine-tuning, training)", "R&D (product discovery, advanced application testing, process engineering)", "Sensory analysis (descriptive analysis, time intensity, discrimination testing, threshold testing)", "Spice extraction", "Vacuum fractionation for hop oils", "Regulatory compliance support", "Custom flavor development"], "industries": ["Beverages", "Fats & Oils", "Flavors & Seasoning Blends", "Meat & Poultry", "Noodles", "Pickles", "Plant-Based Proteins", "Refrigerated & Prepared Foods", "Sauces, Dressings & Condiments", "Snacks"], "materials": ["Rosemary", "Capsicum", "Hops", "Spices", "Natural colorants"], "equipment": ["Gas chromatography mass spectrometer", "Vacuum fractionation system", "Don Berdahl Center for New Technology", "SPICE Lab at Wageningen University", "Spice Processing Center (Kalamazoo)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated supply chain from seed to shelf", "Certified B Corp meeting highest social and environmental standards", "Family-owned business", "Global R&D and application centers (Don Berdahl Center, SPICE Lab)", "Sensory panel trained on Spectrum Method"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958 in Kala