o additives/preservatives -> /", "Ships nationwide -> /", "Featured on Martha Stewart, Food Finds, Travel Channel -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kenyon''s Grist Mill is the oldest manufacturing business in Rhode Island, dating back to 1696.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kenyon-s-grist-mill' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kerr Industries of Texas was founded in 1952 in Grand Prairie, Texas. The company began with a focus on creativity, common sense, and putting customers'' needs first, principles that continue to guide its operations.

The company specializes in upfitting emergency and commercial vehicles, providing integration engineering, prisoner containment systems, push bars, K-9 transport, ballistic protection, auxiliary battery systems, and repainting services. As a Tier 1 supplier, Kerr maintains production quality and quality systems equivalent to OEM standards. The firm has upfitted hundreds of thousands of emergency vehicles, offering turn-key solutions for single units and large fleets while maintaining FMVSS/CMVSS compliance and preserving original factory warranties. Its technicians are EVT certified, and the company also operates as a retail and wholesale distributor of automotive parts, installing custom equipment packages at its facilities.

Kerr serves law enforcement, emergency services, fire services, and commercial vehicle fleets. Its customers include front-line officers and agencies requiring reliable, ready-for-patrol vehicles. The company provides vehicle-specific option guides and engineering support to ensure equipment integration meets operational needs.

Kerr differentiates itself through its Integration Engineering methodology, which bridges aftermarket equipment manufacturers and automotive OEMs. The company emphasizes quick turnaround, cost-effective solutions without compromising quality, and technical support throughout the vehicle lifecycle. Its READY FOR PATROL packages are designed to ensure all specified equipment works properly in new or existing vehicles.', certifications=ARRAY['EVT certified','FMVSS/CMVSS compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Integration Engineering", "Prisoner Containment", "Push-Bar Installation", "K9 Products", "Ballistic Protection", "Turn-Key Vehicle Solutions", "Auxiliary Battery System Installation", "Repainting Services", "Automotive Parts Distribution", "Custom Equipment Package Design", "FMVSS/CMVSS Compliance Verification", "EVT Certified Upfitting", "Technical Support", "Vehicle Specific Option Guides"], "industries": ["Law Enforcement", "Emergency Services", "Fire Services", "Commercial Vehicles"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick turnaround on single vehicles and large fleets", "FMVSS/CMVSS compliance maintained on every upfit", "OE factory warranty preserved", "EVT certified installation technicians", "Integration Engineering methodology bridging aftermarket and OEM"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1952 -> db", "Headquarters in Grand Prairie, Texas -> db", "Industries served: Law Enforcement, Emergency Services, Fire Services, Commercial Vehicles -> db", "Capabilities: Integration Engineering, Prisoner Containment, Push-Bars, K9 Products, Ballistic Protection, Turn-Key Vehicle Solutions, Auxiliary Battery System, K-9 Transport, Repainting Services -> db", "Upfitted hundreds of thousands of emergency vehicles -> page /", "EVT certified technicians -> page /", "FMVSS/CMVSS compliance maintained -> page /", "Integration Engineering methodology -> page /", "READY FOR PATROL packages -> page /", "Tie