UPDATE companies SET description='Kodiak Assembly Solutions, LP was founded in 2004 in Austin, Texas, to provide electronic manufacturing services (EMS) to original equipment manufacturers worldwide. The company operates from a 60,000-square-foot facility in Austin and has grown into a significant participant in the EMS sector through its engineering staff and manufacturing capacity.

The company specializes in surface mount technology (SMT) assembly, mixed-technology PCB assembly, box build assembly, and system integration. It supports both tin-lead (Sn-Pb) and lead-free (RoHS) soldering chemistries to IPC-A-610 Class 2 and 3 standards. Production spans prototype through low, medium, and high volumes, with an ERP-driven material management system tracking more than 40,000 components across turnkey, consigned, and hybrid inventory models. In-house testing includes automated optical inspection, X-ray analysis, flying probe verification, and functional test.

Kodiak serves high-reliability industries including medical and biotechnology, Internet of Things (IoT) devices, RF and wireless communications, industrial control systems, energy applications, oil and gas, security, and LED lighting. Its customer base consists of OEMs requiring turnkey electronics manufacturing and high-mix PCB assembly.

The company emphasizes quality and on-time delivery, citing a 97 percent on-time delivery rate over the previous five years. It holds ISO 9001:2015, UL, CSA, and ITAR certifications, and participates in the Electronic Industry Citizenship Coalition. Engineering support and design-for-manufacturability services are offered through a single purchase order to streamline development.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL','CSA','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface mount technology (SMT) assembly", "Mixed-technology PCB assembly", "Box build assembly", "System integration", "New product introduction (NPI) support", "Material management (turnkey, consigned, hybrid)", "Component sourcing and procurement", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection", "Flying probe testing", "Functional testing", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Design for assembly (DFA)", "Engineering support", "Prototyping", "Low-volume production", "Medium-volume production", "High-volume production", "Sn-Pb (tin-lead) assembly", "RoHS (lead-free) assembly", "Wave soldering (RoHS and non-RoHS)"], "industries": ["Medical and biotechnology", "Internet of Things (IoT)", "RF and wireless communications", "Industrial control systems", "Energy applications", "Oil and gas", "Security", "LED lighting", "Microprocessor embedded computer assemblies"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SMT automation lines", "X-ray inspection system", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) system", "Flying probe tester", "Wave soldering equipment (RoHS and non-RoHS)"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production; low, medium, and high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["97% on-time delivery rate over the past five years", "ISO 9001:2015, UL, CSA, and ITAR certified facility", "60,000 sq ft facility with advanced SMT automation and X-ray/AOI inspection", "ERP-driven material management tracking 40,000+ components", "Supports both Sn-Pb and RoHS assembly to IPC-A-610 Class 2 