UPDATE companies SET description='LJ Design and Manufacturing operates from Brookfield, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1844. The company began as a sewing contractor and has evolved into a technical soft goods manufacturer serving medical and industrial OEMs.

The firm provides end-to-end product development, from design and engineering through textile cutting and contract sewing to full-scale manufacturing. Its single Brookfield facility houses programmable CNC fabric cutters, die presses, automated trim cutters, and a diverse array of industrial sewing machines capable of bar tack, cover stitch, lockstitch, overlock, and other specialized stitch types. The company handles projects from prototype to mass production, though specific volume figures are not disclosed.

Customers span medical device OEMs, industrial equipment makers, commercial furniture, transportation, and military/government sectors. Representative projects include crane operator vests, thermal incubator covers, and 24/7 chairs. The product portfolio covers medical devices, protective gear, upholstered products, equipment covers, compression garments, custom bags and cases, pads and cushions, and industrial curtains.

The company differentiates itself through nearly two centuries of experience, ISO compliance, FDA registration as a medical device contractor, and a made-in-USA single-site operation. It emphasizes an in-house engineering team that optimizes designs for manufacturability, a low-turnover workforce, continuous improvement programs, and global textile sourcing relationships for materials such as Kevlar, Nomex, coated fabrics, and foams.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO standards compliant','FDA Registered Medical Device Contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product design", "Product engineering", "CNC fabric cutting", "Die cutting", "Hot knife cutting", "Cold knife cutting", "Industrial sewing", "Medical sewing", "Custom sewing", "Bar tack stitching", "Box X stitching", "Computerized pattern sewing", "Cover stitch", "Cylinder bed lockstitch", "Double needle lockstitch", "Double needle chain stitch", "Overlock serging", "Post bed single needle lockstitch", "Post bed double needle lockstitch", "Single needle lockstitch", "Walking foot sewing", "Zig-zag stitching", "Upholstery", "First article inspection"], "industries": ["Medical", "Industrial", "Commercial Furniture", "Transportation", "Military/Government", "OEM"], "materials": ["Reinforced coated vinyl", "Laminated vinyl", "Expanded vinyl", "PVC coated polyester", "Urethane coated nylon", "Silicone coated fiberglass", "Leather", "Silicon", "Kevlar\u00ae", "Nomex\u00ae", "Knit fabrics", "Nylons", "Hypalon", "Foam", "High temperature materials"], "equipment": ["CNC fabric cutting machines", "Programmable automated cutters", "Die presses", "Automated trim cutting machines", "Industrial sewing machines (bar tack, box X, computerized pattern, cover stitch, cylinder bed lockstitch, double needle lockstitch, double needle chain stitch, overlock serger, post bed single needle lockstitch, post bed double needle lockstitch, single needle lockstitch, walking foot, zig-zag)", "Hot knife cutters", "Cold knife cutters"], "vo