UPDATE companies SET description='Liberty Plastics Molding Corporation Inc. is a family-owned injection molding and mold building company based in Bellevue, Kentucky. Founded in 1973 as Liberty Products Inc. by Homer and Marlene Gemmer, the business began in a small building on Liberty Street in Newport, Kentucky. Homer Gemmer, formerly a model shop supervisor at a major toy manufacturer in the Cincinnati area, started a machine and mold shop that grew into injection molding. The company relocated to its current 56,000-square-foot facility in Bellevue on April 2, 1993.

The company operates 15 injection molding machines ranging from 75 to 550 tons, supporting both short and long production runs. In-house mold building covers aluminum and steel tooling, single or multi-cavity, from prototype to full production. Secondary operations and blanket order programs allow customers to avoid multi-sourcing and store parts for up to a year. Materials processed include high- and low-density polyethylene, polypropylene, HIPS, ABS, Delrin, nylon, polycarbonate, polyurethane, PVC (rigid and flexible), CPVC, and PVDF.

Liberty serves a broad range of sectors including conveyor and packaging, power and utility, bowling, chemical pump, casket, furniture, pet supply, towing and recovery, food, toy, medical, and automotive industries. Customers such as Wayne F. in conveyor and belting packaging, Tom V. across multiple industries, and Patrick F. in the bearing industry have relied on the company for made-to-order parts.

The Gemmer family’s multi-generational ownership — now led by third-generation President Jeff Jr. Gemmer and CFO Jaclyn Gemmer Thompson — emphasizes hands-on service and continuity. The company highlights its total in-house capabilities, central Midwest location for lower freight costs, and a commitment to quality, price, and delivery as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Injection mold building (aluminum and steel)", "Secondary operations", "Blanket order management", "Prototype tooling", "Production tooling", "Short-run production", "Long-run production", "Material selection consulting"], "industries": ["Conveyor and Packaging", "Power and Utility", "Bowling", "Chemical Pump", "Casket", "Furniture", "Pet Supply", "Towing and Recovery", "Food", "Toy", "Medical", "Automotive", "Bearing"], "materials": ["High-density polyethylene (HDPE)", "Low-density polyethylene (LDPE)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "High-impact polystyrene (HIPS)", "Acrylonitrile butadiene styrene (ABS)", "Delrin (acetal)", "Nylon", "Polycarbonate (PC)", "Polyurethane (PU)", "PVC rigid and flexible", "CPVC", "PVDF"], "equipment": ["TRAK DPM RX3 CNC machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Total in-house capabilities from mold building to secondary operations", "Central Midwest location reducing freight costs to East and West coasts", "Family-owned since 1973 with third-generation leadership", "Blanket order program storing parts for up to a year", "15 injection molding machines ranging 75 to 550 tons"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1973 by Homer and Marlene Gemmer -> /about", "Family-owned since 1973 -> /about, /", "Location Bellevue, KY -> /about", "56,000 sq ft building -> /about", "15 injection molding machines 75-550 ton -> /services", "Materials list (HDPE, LDPE, PP, HIPS, ABS, Delrin, Nylon, PC, PU, PVC, CPVC, PVDF) -> /services", "Industries served (Conveyor, Power, Bowling, Chemical Pump, Cask