UPDATE companies SET description='Liberty Steel & Wire operates a large integrated steel mill in Peoria, Illinois. The business traces its roots back more than 125 years and today functions as part of Liberty Steel USA, a family of companies headquartered in New York that produces fabricated wire products, reinforcing bar, and prestressed concrete strand.

The Peoria facility melts, refines, and casts steel on site, producing roughly 700,000 tons annually. A continuous billet caster feeds a rod mill equipped with a Morgan No‑Twist finishing mill and retarded cooling, while 22 drawing machines handle wire drawing to customer specifications. Finished output includes billets, rod, rebar, industrial wire, PC strand, welded wire mesh, and the Red Brand line of agricultural fencing.

Customers span construction (cast‑in‑place and precast concrete), infrastructure, industrial OEMs, agriculture, and retail consumers. The company’s welded wire reinforcement is certified to ASTM standards for precast and cast‑in‑place applications, and its Red Brand fencing is marketed as the only agricultural fence made entirely in the U.S. from start to finish.

Liberty emphasizes its domestic supply chain: every step from scrap processing through final packaging occurs at its own U.S. facilities, making its products Buy America compliant. The mill offers customized steel grades — over 20 variations within the 1008 classification alone — and holds ISO 9001 certification and ISO 17025 (A2LA) accreditation for its testing laboratory.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 17025 (A2LA)','ASTM Standard Specifications','Buy America compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Welded wire reinforcement", "Engineered wire products", "Bar products", "Billet casting", "Rod rolling (Morgan No\u2011Twist finishing mill)", "Wire drawing (22 drawing machines)", "Rebar production", "PC strand manufacturing", "Agricultural fencing (Red Brand)", "Custom steel grade development", "ASTM standard compliance", "ISO 9001 quality management", "ISO 17025 (A2LA) accredited testing"], "industries": ["Construction (cast\u2011in\u2011place, precast)", "Infrastructure", "Industrial OEM", "Agriculture", "Retail consumer"], "materials": ["High carbon steel", "CHQ grade steel", "1008 steel grades", "Recycled steel scrap"], "equipment": ["Continuous billet caster", "Morgan No\u2011Twist finishing mill", "Retarded cooling system", "22 wire drawing machines"], "volume": "700,000 tons annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% American\u2011made, Buy America compliant", "Integrated mill controls every step from scrap melting to finished product", "Custom steel grades (over 20 variations of 1008 steel)", "ISO 9001 certified quality system and ISO 17025 (A2LA) accredited lab", "ASTM\u2011certified welded wire reinforcement for precast and cast\u2011in\u2011place"], "facts_used": ["Location: Peoria, Illinois -> db", "Over 125 years in steel industry -> page \"/\"", "Produces 700,000 tons of steel annually -> page \"/\"", "Continuous billet caster, Morgan No\u2011Twist finishing mill, 22 drawing machines -> page \"/\"", "Welded wire reinforcement certified to ASTM standards -> db description and page \"/services\"", "Red Brand agricultural fencing made entirely in U.S. -> page \"/\"", "ISO 9001 certification -> db certifications and page \"/\"", "ISO 17025 (A2LA) accreditation -> page \"/\"", "Buy America compliant, 100% American\u2011made -> page \"/\"", "Custom steel grades, over 20 variations of 1008 steel -> page \"/\"", "Part of Liberty Steel USA family of companies -> page \"/about-us\""], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "LEWP is a leading manufacturer of welded wire reinforcement for the Cast in Place and Precast Industries.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='liberty-steel-wire-products-peoria' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Life Science Outsourcing, Inc. was established in 1997 in Anaheim, California, to provide contract manufacturing services to emerging medical device companies. The company operates three FDA‑registered facilities totaling over 125,000 square feet: its headquarters in Anaheim, California (80,000+ sq ft with eight cleanrooms), a packaging and validation site in Salem, New Hampshire, and an assembly and kitting operation in Zona Franca Coyol, Alajuela, Costa Rica.

The company provides end‑to‑end medical device contract manufacturing, including cleanroom assembly (Class 5–8), packaging validation (ISO 11607), sterilization (EO, gamma, e‑beam), cleaning and decontamination, and fulfillment. Its 12 cleanrooms, a Class 7 dry room, and low‑humidity areas support bioabsorbable polymer processing. With over 125,000 square feet of FDA‑registered space across three sites, LSO handles projects from prototype through commercial scale, having supported more than 820 product launches for over 1,400 clients in 25 years.

LSO serves medical device companies across orthopedics, cardiovascular and electrophysiology, neuromodulation, diagnostics (IVD/POC), minimally invasive devices, cardiac rhythm management, respiratory, gastrointestinal, dental implants, specialty kits, and oncology. Its customers range from early‑stage startups — such as a breast‑biopsy company that used LSO for turnkey assembly, packaging validation, and sterilization until its 2010 acquisition, and an orthopedic startup that relied on LSO for packaging and sterilization validation before a $130 million acquisition in 2004 — to established OEMs consolidating vendors. The company also supported rapid COVID‑19 swab production, achieving commercial distribution in four weeks.

LSO differentiates itself by consolidating assembly, packaging, validation, sterilization, and distribution under a single FDA‑registered, ISO 13485‑certified quality system, eliminating vendor handoffs and reducing audit burden. The company states its model was created to give emerging medical device firms access to cleanroom infrastructure, quality systems, and regulatory guidance without building their own facilities, enabling faster time to market and lower supply‑chain risk.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA CDRH Registration (Contract Manufacturer, Contract Sterilizer)','ISO 13485:2016','ISO/IEC 17025:2017','ISO 11607','ISO 11135:2014','ISO 11137','ISO 17665-1:2006','ISO 10993','21 CFR 820','Japan Minister of Health registration','ISTA Certified Package Testing Laboratory','California Board of Pharmacy Drug Wholesaler License','State of California Device and Drug Manufacturing Licenses']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cleanroom assembly (Class 5\u20138)", "Packaging validation (ISO 11607)", "Sterilization (EO, gamma, e\u2011beam)", "Cleaning and decontamination of reusable devices", "Fulfillment and distribution", "Diagnostic reagent blister design and manufacturing", "Medical device assembly", "Medical package testing", "Quality incubator support for startups", "Component sourcing and inspection", "Packaging and labeling", "Kitting and bundling", "Regulatory compliance and validation", "Facility utilization (daily cleanroom rental)", "Low\u2011humidity manufacturing", "Solvent scouring for bioabsorbable polymers"], "industries": ["Orthopedics", "Cardiovascular and Electrophysiology", "Neuromodulation", "Diagnostics (IVD/POC)", "Minimally Invasive Devices", "Cardiac Rhythm Management", "Respiratory", "Gastrointestinal", "Dental Implants", "Specialty Kits", "Oncology"], "materials": ["Bioabsorbable polymers", "Diagnostic reagents"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to commercial production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Consolidated assembly, packaging, validation, sterilization, and distribution under one quality system", "50% fewer vendor audits", "30% faster time to market", "Facility Utilization Option offering daily cleanroom rental for prototypes", "Pre\u2011validated packaging solutions and quick\u2011turn sterilization"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1997 -> /about", "Headquarters in Anaheim, California -> /about", "Three facilities totaling 125,000+ sq ft -> /about", "12 cleanrooms Class 5\u20138 -> /about", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /about", "FDA registered -> /about", "ISO 17025 accredited packaging lab -> /about", "Services: assembly, packaging, validation, sterilization, cleaning, fulfillment -> /services", "Industries served: orthopedics, cardiovascular, neuromodulation, diagnostics, etc. -> /about", "820+ product launches supported -> /", "50% fewer vendor audits -> /", "30% faster time to market -> /", "Facility Utilization Option (daily cleanroom rental) -> /about", "COVID-19 swab project completed in 4 weeks -> /", "Breast biopsy startup acquired 2010 -> /", "Orthopedic startup acquired for ~$130M in 2004 -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Life Science Outsourcing (LSO) is a full-service medical device contract manufacturer", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["Japan Minister of Health registration"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='life-science-outsourcing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Life Scientific, Inc. was founded in 1992 in St. Louis, Missouri, as a manufacturers'' representative firm serving the pharmaceutical equipment market. The company operates from its headquarters with additional branches in Illinois, Minnesota, and Canada.

The firm represents eight equipment manufacturers — including Aseptic Enclosures, Cozzoli Machine Co., Engineered BioSystems, Environmental Specialties, Fedegari Autoclavi, HICOF, Newman Labelling, and Vibrac — providing access to gloveboxes, isolators, filling and capping systems, bioreactors, stability chambers, autoclaves, track-and-trace systems, labeling machines, and cap torque testers. Life Scientific''s team of manufacturers'' representatives and industrial sales representatives has consulted on more than 5,000 equipment opportunities, and the company leverages a network of partner organizations with a collective staff of over 1,000 professionals offering project management, engineering, validation, technical support, and training.

