UPDATE companies SET description='Lomont Molding LLC was founded in 1982 in Mount Pleasant, Iowa, where it continues to operate a high-capacity facility running 24 hours a day. The company began as a structural foam molding operation focused on large-format parts and has since expanded into a multi-process plastic molding enterprise.

Today Lomont provides injection molding, blow molding, structural foam, over-molding, nitrogen gas-assist molding, and in-mold decorating, supported by in-house engineering, tooling, quality assurance, and secondary operations.

The company serves diverse markets through its proprietary product lines: Paragon Products supplies concrete and rebar accessories to commercial highway, ready-mix, pre-cast, and concrete testing sectors; Lomont IMT produces safety signage and identification products using patented in-mold technology; and R&D Molders brings decades of blow molding and injection molding experience to medical, consumer, electronics, and energy applications.

Lomont emphasizes its ability to adapt through continuous technology investment — adding gas-assist, over-molding, and in-mold labeling capabilities — and its ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system with ERP-driven traceability, PPAP documentation, and in-process inspection. The company states its mission is to provide quality, service, and innovation that exceed customer expectations.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Blow molding", "Structural foam molding", "Over-molding", "Nitrogen gas-assist molding", "In-mold decorating (IMD)", "In-mold labeling", "Engineering and design support", "Tooling design and construction", "Quality assurance and inspection", "Secondary operations", "Assembly", "PPAP documentation", "Control plan development", "Inspection reporting", "Certificate of compliance issuance"], "industries": ["Medical", "Consumer products", "Electronics", "Energy", "Commercial highway construction", "Concrete testing laboratories", "Ready-mix concrete", "Pre-cast construction", "Safety marking and signage"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "Thermoplastic elastomers (TPE)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete in-house engineering, tooling, decorating, quality assurance, and secondary operations", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system with IQMS ERP traceability", "24/7 operation from a high-capacity Iowa facility", "Proprietary product lines: Paragon Products, Lomont IMT, R&D Molders", "Decades of experience across injection, blow, structural foam, and gas-assist molding"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 in Mount Pleasant, Iowa -> /about", "Operates 24/7 from high-capacity facility in southeast Iowa -> /about", "Core processes: injection molding, blow molding, structural foam, over-molding, nitrogen gas-assist, in-mold decorating -> /", "In-house engineering, tooling, quality assurance, secondary operations -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with IQMS ERP traceability -> /quality", "Proprietary lines: Paragon Products (concrete/rebar accessories), Lomont IMT (safety signage), R&D Molders (blow/injection molding) -> /about", "Paragon serves commercial highway, ready-mix, pre-cast, concrete test labs -> /about", "R&D Molders serves medical, consumer, electronics, energy -> /about", "History timeline: 1982 structural foam, 1989 injection molding, 2000 gas-assist/over-molding, 2003 in-mold decorating, 2017 blow molding via R&D Molders acquisition -> /about", "Processes thermoplastic resins including TPE for over-molding -> /about, /", "Quality system includes PPAP, control plans, inspection reports, certificates of compliance -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Lomont Molding, LLC is a premier plastic molder offering complete in-house services including engineering, tooling, in-mold technologies, decorating, quality assurance, and secondary operations.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lomont-molding-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Louisiana Plastic Industries was founded in 1973 by Sidney R. Wilhite in West Monroe, Louisiana. Today, the company operates under the leadership of Wilhite''s sons, John Mark Wilhite and Ross Wilhite Jr., who continue as owners.

The manufacturer runs an 80,000-square-foot facility on four acres, equipped with 13 advanced blown film extrusion lines. These lines produce high-density, low-density, and linear low-density polyethylene films, as well as polypropylene, in widths up to 80 inches. The operation includes custom film blending, pre-slitting, perforating, and tubing, delivering single-wound and two-ply sheeting tailored for multi-wall bag production and other industrial packaging needs.

Primary customers serve the multi-wall bag industry, with films also used in roofing, food service, and specialty applications. The company''s strategic location alongside the CPKC Railroad, supported by eight on-site silos and a dedicated truck fleet, enables direct delivery across the United States.

Louisiana Plastic Industries emphasizes rigorous quality controls, including FDA-compliant virgin resins, gluability treatment, and continuous monitoring of gauge, width, moisture vapor transmission, and oxygen transmission rates. Every order is inspected during production, and the company guarantees on-time delivery backed by its own logistics network.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown film extrusion", "Custom film blending", "Pre-slitting", "Perforating", "Polyethylene film tubing", "Single-wound film sheeting", "Two-ply film sheeting", "Gluability treatment", "Gauge and width inspection", "Moisture vapor transmission rate (MVTR) testing", "Oxygen transmission rate (OTR) testing", "Railcar unloading and silo storage", "Truckload delivery"], "industries": ["Multi-wall bag manufacturing", "Roofing", "Food service packaging", "Industrial packaging", "Specialty film applications"], "materials": ["High Density Polyethylene (HDPE)", "Low Density Polyethylene (LDPE)", "Linear Low Density Polyethylene (LLDPE)", "Polypropylene", "Virgin FDA-approved resins", "Custom film blends"], "equipment": ["13 advanced blown film extrusion lines", "Automatic trim and treatment/millage monitoring equipment", "Micrometer gauge measurement tools", "Roll circumference measurement system", "Eight on-site resin silos", "Dedicated truck fleet"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Strategic rail access via CPKC Railroad with eight on-site silos for efficient bulk handling", "Dedicated fleet of trucks and drivers for direct, on-time delivery", "13 blown film extrusion lines enabling flexible, short-lead-time production", "In-line quality inspection every 30\u201345 minutes with automatic equipment warnings", "FDA-compliant virgin resins and made-in-USA manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1973 by Sidney R. Wilhite -> /about", "Located in West Monroe, Louisiana -> /", "Family-owned, current owners John Mark Wilhite and Ross Wilhi