UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1977 in Auburn, Maine, M & P Auto Parts has spent decades serving the region from its facility on Merrow Road. The business began as a local auto parts supplier and grew into a full-service salvage yard that purchases, dismantles, and resells functional components from both working and nonworking vehicles.

The company operates a salvage yard that stocks new and used auto parts for foreign and domestic cars and trucks, including items such as air pumps, carburetors, fenders, headlights, rear doors, and trunk lids. It also provides junk car removal — available only in the Auburn and Lewiston areas — and offers an online multi-part search tool for customers to locate inventory. A 90-day warranty covers mechanical parts, while electrical parts carry a 30-day warranty.

Its service area includes Auburn, Lewiston, Portland, Augusta, Waterville, Brunswick, Sanford, Scarborough, Biddeford, Bangor, and surrounding communities. The yard caters to those needing affordable replacement parts for everything from daily drivers to rare classic vehicles.

