UPDATE companies SET description='MV Circuit Breakers began in 1998 when Brad Goebel and Steve Wallem founded the company, then called MV Liquidators, in a friend''s garage in Mission Viejo, California. The pair traveled across the country purchasing new circuit breaker inventory from contracting firms to offer customers the lowest possible prices, and their supplier relationships expanded the available stock over time.

The business operates as a distributor of residential and commercial circuit breakers and electrical components, carrying thousands of SKUs from brands such as Siemens, Square D, Eaton, Cutler‑Hammer, GE, Murray, and obsolete lines including Zinsco, Pushmatic, Challenger, and Federal Pacific. A retail location opened in 2005 at 23881 Via Fabricante in Mission Viejo. The company sells primarily new breakers alongside professionally tested used units, offers same‑day delivery in Southern California, same‑day shipping nationwide, free shipping on orders over $150, a one‑year warranty, and in‑store pickup.

Reviews highlight the ability to source hard‑to‑find breakers within 24 hours and provide emergency support, with one electrician noting he refers all his contacts to the company.

